.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt REBOOT 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm reboot ,
.Nm halt ,
.Nm poweroff
.Nd stop, restart or power off the system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl lnpq
.Nm
.Fl r
.Op Oo Ar type : Oc Ns Ar special
.Nm halt
.Op Fl lnpq
.Nm poweroff
.Op Fl lnq
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm ,
.Nm halt
and
.Nm poweroff
utilities restart the system, stop it, or turn the power off.
They are one program; its name selects the action.
.Pp
By default the request goes to
.Xr init 8 ,
which runs
.Pa /etc/rc.shutdown ,
terminates every process, synchronizes the file systems and then carries
it out.
The request is a signal to process 1:
.Dv SIGINT
to restart,
.Dv SIGUSR1
to halt, and
.Dv SIGUSR2
to power off.
.Fl r
gives the kernel the new root
.Pq Xr reboot 2 Ns 's Dv RB_REROOT ,
which asks init with
.Dv SIGPWR .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl l
Accepted for compatibility; there is no system log to suppress.
.It Fl n
With
.Fl q ,
do not synchronize the file systems first.
.It Fl p
Power off instead of restarting or halting.
.It Fl q
Do not involve
.Xr init 8 :
synchronize the file systems and call
.Xr reboot 2
at once.
No services are stopped and no process is warned.
.It Fl r Op Oo Ar type : Oc Ns Ar special
Switch the root file system without restarting the kernel: everything is
shut down as for a restart, then every file system is unmounted, the file
system of
.Ar type
.Pq Cm oxfs No by default
on device
.Ar special
is mounted as the root, read-only as at boot, and
.Xr init 8
starts on it, running its
.Pa /etc/rc .
Without
.Ar special ,
the root
.Pa /etc/fstab
names.
The device is checked before anything stops.
If the new root can't be mounted, the old one is mounted again and init
starts on it.
Nothing survives the switch but the processes' absence: a
.Xr tmpfs 5
loses its contents, and
.Xr devfs 4
and
.Pa /proc
are mounted afresh.
.El
.Pp
Only the superuser may use these utilities.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
On success with
.Fl q
nothing returns.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reboot 2 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr shutdown 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.At v6 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
.Sh BUGS
Until
.Pa /sbin/init
runs as process 1, only
.Fl q
restarts or stops the system.
